  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The number of real values of <math><mi>&#955;</mi></math> for which the system of linear equations,&nbsp;<math><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>,&nbsp;<math><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, has infinitely many solutions, is:</p>",
    "image": null
